meta {
  name: Record juz progress
  type: http
  seq: 11
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/khatm/assignments/:assignmentId/progress
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

params:path {
  assignmentId: uuid
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "progress_percent": 60,
    "previous_percent": 50,
    "source": "IN_APP | ADMIN_OVERRIDE | AUTO_TRACKING",
    "note": null
  }
}

docs {
  Replaces: useUpdateProgress (khatm_progress_updates ledger insert +
  khatm_juz_assignments.progress_percent update; DB triggers currently derive
  started_at / completed_at / status transitions — that logic moves into this
  endpoint or equivalent triggers).

  Authorization (from RLS khatm_progress_updates_insert):
  - the assignment's own participant may record IN_APP or AUTO_TRACKING
  - admin/co-admin of the group may record ADMIN_OVERRIDE for any assignment
  - anyone else: 403

  AUTO_TRACKING is sent by the Quran reader while reading inside the
  assignment's page range — same authorization as IN_APP, only the source
  label differs (it renders as "auto-tracked" in history).

  Status transitions to preserve: 0→>0 sets IN_PROGRESS + started_at;
  reaching 100 sets COMPLETED + completed_at; group completion is detected
  when all 30 juz are COMPLETED (currently a DB trigger) and must emit the
  group-completed event (see events.bru).

  Response 200: updated assignment object.
}
